                <pb facs="0796" n="784" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg784"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/643: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sterling</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-02T12:00:00+01:00">December 2,
                            1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 2—8:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>239. The Swedish Government on November 30 made a formal protest to the British
                    and French Governments against the blockade of German exports. This was done the
                    Foreign Office states to support the other neutral powers that have made
                    protests. The Foreign Office adds that it expects very shortly to have an
                    arrangement with Great Britain whereby Swedish commerce will suffer very
                    little.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
